# simplegraph-agentic — merge behavior for the graph.
#
# Parallel agents and feature branches append nodes to these list files. A
# plain merge conflicts on nearly every concurrent add, which pushes people to
# defer graph updates — the opposite of what the graph needs. `merge=union` is
# a built-in git driver (no config required) that keeps BOTH sides' lines, so
# two branches that each appended a node merge cleanly.
#
# After any merge that touched these files, run:
#   sg reindex                          # rebuild the derived Quick Index
#   core/scripts/consistency_check.sh   # catches any duplicate IDs union produced
#
# NOT union-merged, on purpose:
#   graph_index.md   — a derived table; regenerate it with `sg reindex` instead.
#   components/*.md   — one node per file, so branches touch different files.

regressions.md                  merge=union
invariants.md                   merge=union
decisions.md                    merge=union
watchlists.md                   merge=union
anti_patterns.md                merge=union
archive/resolved_regressions.md merge=union
